<title>POLAND: Bourse suspends Espebepe trade March 14.</title>
<headline>Bourse suspends Espebepe trade March 14.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Warsaw bourse will suspend Polish construction firm Espebepe SA trade on Friday, when creditors of the debt-ridden company meet to decide on a possible debt write-off deal, the bourse's president said.</p>
<p>&quot;I would like to announce that on March 14 Espebepe trade will be suspended as there will be creditors' meeting on the day,&quot; Wieslaw Rozlucki said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Espebepe, which has about 75 million zloty debts, earlier said it would go bankrupt if its creditors did not agree to a deep debt-write-off.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
